'''Season thirty-one''' of ''[[Dancing with the Stars (American TV series)|Dancing with the Stars]]'' premiered on [[Disney+]] on September 19, 2022,<ref>{{cite press release|url=http://thefutoncritic.com/video/2022/08/03/video-disneyplus-reveals-anticipated-premiere-dates-and-trailers-at-television-critics-association-summer-2022-press-tour-840514/20220803disney01/|title=Video: Disney+ Reveals Anticipated Premiere Dates and Trailers at Television Critics Association Summer 2022 Press Tour|publisher=[[Disney+]]|via=[[The Futon Critic]]|date=August 3, 2022|access-date=August 3, 2022}}</ref><ref>{{cite web|url=https://deadline.com/2022/08/dancing-with-the-stars-premiere-disney-plus-september-1235084406/|title=''Dancing With The Stars'' Gets Disney+ Premiere Date|work=[[Deadline Hollywood]]|author=Lynette Rice|date=August 3, 2022|access-date=August 3, 2022|archive-date=August 3, 2022|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20220803171241/https://deadline.com/2022/08/dancing-with-the-stars-premiere-disney-plus-september-1235084406/|url-status=live}}</ref> and concluded on November 21, 2022.<ref>{{cite web|url=https://www.tvline.com/lists/dancing-with-the-stars-recap-season-31-finalists-revealed-top-4/|title=''Dancing With the Stars'': The Finalists Are Set! Which Duos Made the Top 4?|work=[[TVLine]]|author=Rebecca Iannucci|date=November 14, 2022|access-date=November 17, 2022|archive-date=November 17, 2022|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20221117035535/https://tvline.com/lists/dancing-with-the-stars-recap-season-31-finalists-revealed-top-4/|url-status=live}}</ref> This season marked the first live competition show to air on the streaming platform and the only season to not air on [[American Broadcasting Company|ABC]].<ref>{{cite web|url=https://deadline.com/2022/04/dancing-with-the-stars-leaving-abc-disney-plus-season-31-1234996886/|title=''Dancing With The Stars'' Moving To Disney+ In Stunning Move After 16 Years On ABC|work=[[Deadline Hollywood]]|author=Lynette Rice|date=April 8, 2022|access-date=August 3, 2022|archive-date=May 22, 2022|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20220522191502/https://deadline.com/2022/04/dancing-with-the-stars-leaving-abc-disney-plus-season-31-1234996886/|url-status=live}}</ref> [[Tyra Banks]] returned as host, while [[Dancing with the Stars (American TV series) season 19|season nineteen]] champion [[Alfonso Ribeiro]] joined as co-host.

Social media personality [[Charli D'Amelio]] and [[Mark Ballas]] were crowned the champions, while ''[[The Bachelorette (American TV series)|The Bachelorette]]'' star [[Gabby Windey]] and [[Val Chmerkovskiy]] finished in second place, comedian [[Wayne Brady]] and [[Witney Carson]] finished in third place, and drag queen [[Shangela]] and [[Gleb Savchenko]] finished in fourth.

This marked the last season for host [[Tyra Banks]]<ref>{{cite web|url=https://deadline.com/2023/03/tyra-banks-leaving-dancing-with-the-stars-1235302893/|title=Tyra Banks Is Leaving ''Dancing With The Stars''|work=[[Deadline Hollywood]]|author=Lynette Rice|date=March 17, 2023|access-date=March 17, 2023|archive-date=March 19, 2023|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20230319225118/https://deadline.com/2023/03/tyra-banks-leaving-dancing-with-the-stars-1235302893/|url-status=live}}</ref> and longtime judge [[Len Goodman]], who retired at the conclusion of the season, prior to his death five months later.<ref>{{cite web|url=https://deadline.com/2023/04/len-goodman-dies-former-strictly-come-dancing-dancing-with-the-stars-judge-was-78-1235334683/|title=Len Goodman Dies: Former ''Strictly Come Dancing'' & ''Dancing With The Stars'' Judge Was 78|work=[[Deadline Hollywood]]|author=Max Goldbart|date=April 24, 2023|access-date=April 24, 2023|archive-date=April 24, 2023|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20230424084437/https://deadline.com/2023/04/len-goodman-dies-former-strictly-come-dancing-dancing-with-the-stars-judge-was-78-1235334683/|url-status=live}}</ref>

==Cast==

=== Couples ===
This season featured sixteen celebrity contestants. On August 25, 2022, it was reported that [[Charli D'Amelio]] and her mother [[Heidi D'Amelio]] would be competing as celebrity participants.<ref>{{cite web|url=https://deadline.com/2022/08/dancing-with-the-stars-tiktok-star-charli-damelio-mom-heidi-season-31-1235100427/|title=''Dancing With The Stars'': TikTok Star Charli D'Amelio & Mom Heidi Joining Season 31|work=[[Deadline Hollywood]]|author=Lynette Rice|date=August 25, 2022|access-date=August 25, 2022|archive-date=August 26, 2022|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20220826075616/https://deadline.com/2022/08/dancing-with-the-stars-tiktok-star-charli-damelio-mom-heidi-season-31-1235100427/|url-status=live}}</ref> Soon after, [[Joseph Baena]], [[Wayne Brady]], [[Daniel Durant]],<ref>{{cite web|url=https://heavy.com/entertainment/dancing-with-the-stars/joseph-baena-season-31-contestant-partner/|title=Son of Famous Actor Set to Compete on DWTS Season 31|work=[[Heavy (website)|Heavy]]|author=Beth Heyn|date=August 26, 2022|access-date=August 26, 2022|archive-date=August 26, 2022|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20220826220550/https://heavy.com/entertainment/dancing-with-the-stars/joseph-baena-season-31-contestant-partner/|url-status=live}}</ref><ref>{{cite web|url=https://heavy.com/entertainment/dancing-with-the-stars/wayne-brady-cast-partner-witney-carson/|title=Superstar Comedian & Actor Announced as DWTS Pro Witney Carson Season 31 Partner|work=[[Heavy (website)|Heavy]]|author=Beth Heyn|date=August 27, 2022|access-date=August 27, 2022|archive-date=August 27, 2022|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20220827171834/https://heavy.com/entertainment/dancing-with-the-stars/wayne-brady-cast-partner-witney-carson/|url-status=live}}</ref> [[Jordin Sparks]],<ref>{{cite web|url=https://heavy.com/entertainment/dancing-with-the-stars/jordin-sparks-season-31-partner-contestant/|title=''American Idol'' Winner Joins DWTS as Season 31 Contestant|work=[[Heavy (website)|Heavy]]|author=Beth Heyn|date=August 30, 2022|access-date=August 31, 2022|archive-date=August 31, 2022|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20220831012903/https://heavy.com/entertainment/dancing-with-the-stars/jordin-sparks-season-31-partner-contestant/|url-status=live}}</ref> [[Gabby Windey]],<ref>{{cite web|url=https://heavy.com/entertainment/dancing-with-the-stars/bachelorette-gabby-windey-season-31/|title=''Bachelorette'' Joins ''Dancing With the Stars'' Season 31 [Report]|work=[[Heavy (website)|Heavy]]|author=Beth Heyn|date=September 2, 2022|access-date=September 2, 2022|archive-date=September 2, 2022|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20220902183815/https://heavy.com/entertainment/dancing-with-the-stars/bachelorette-gabby-windey-season-31/|url-status=live}}</ref> and [[Trevor Donovan]]<ref>{{cite web|url=https://heavy.com/entertainment/dancing-with-the-stars/emma-slater-trevor-donovan-partner-season-31/|title=Emma Slater ''Dancing With the Stars'' Season 31 Partner Revealed|work=[[Heavy (website)|Heavy]]|author=Beth Heyn|date=September 5, 2022|access-date=September 5, 2022|archive-date=September 6, 2022|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20220906014316/https://heavy.com/entertainment/dancing-with-the-stars/emma-slater-trevor-donovan-partner-season-31/|url-status=live}}</ref> were all reported as celebrity participants as well. Charli and Heidi D'Amelio were officially announced as part of the season's cast on September 7,<ref>{{cite magazine|url=https://ew.com/tv/dancing-with-the-stars-season-31-cast-revealed-charli-damelio/|title=Charli D'Amelio and her mom join ''Dancing With the Stars'' season 31 cast: 'I thought they were joking'|magazine=[[Entertainment Weekly]]|author=Joey Nolfi|date=September 7, 2022|access-date=September 7, 2022|archive-date=September 7, 2022|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20220907231813/https://ew.com/tv/dancing-with-the-stars-season-31-cast-revealed-charli-damelio/|url-status=live}}</ref> with the full roster of celebrity participants and their partnerships officially revealed on ''[[Good Morning America]]'' the following day.<ref name="Ribeiro cohost">{{cite web|url=https://www.goodmorningamerica.com/culture/story/alfonso-ribeiro-joins-tyra-banks-host-dancing-stars-86754226|title=Alfonso Ribeiro joins Tyra Banks as co-host for ''Dancing With the Stars'' season 31|work=[[Good Morning America]]|author=Carson Blackwelder|date=July 14, 2022|access-date=August 3, 2022|archive-date=August 15, 2022|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20220815102526/https://www.goodmorningamerica.com/culture/story/alfonso-ribeiro-joins-tyra-banks-host-dancing-stars-86754226|url-status=live}}</ref><ref name="TFC-PR cast">{{cite press release|url=http://www.thefutoncritic.com/news/2022/09/08/dancing-with-the-stars-is-back-for-season-31-with-an-all-new-celebrity-cast-dancing-their-way-to-disneyplus-and-the-mirrorball-trophy-688404/20220908disney02/|title=''Dancing with the Stars'' Is Back for Season 31 with an All-New Celebrity Cast Dancing Their Way to Disney+ and the Mirrorball Trophy|publisher=[[Disney+]]|via=[[The Futon Critic]]|date=September 8, 2022|access-date=September 8, 2022}}</ref> With sixteen couples, this season was tied with [[Dancing with the Stars (American TV series) season 9|season nine]] as having the largest cast in the show's history.<ref>{{cite web|url=https://variety.com/2022/tv/news/dancing-with-the-stars-disney-plus-abc-live-streaming-1235376935/|title=''Dancing With the Stars'' Will Look Different on Disney+: Inside the Show's Jump From ABC to Streaming|work=[[Variety (magazine)|Variety]]|author=Michael Schneider|date=September 19, 2022|access-date=September 20, 2022|archive-date=September 19, 2022|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20220919232204/https://variety.com/2022/tv/news/dancing-with-the-stars-disney-plus-abc-live-streaming-1235376935/|url-status=live}}</ref>

A promo for the season released on August 18 featured professional dancers [[Daniella Karagach]], [[Pasha Pashkov]], [[Artem Chigvintsev]], [[Witney Carson]], [[Brandon Armstrong (dancer)|Brandon Armstrong]], and [[Cheryl Burke]].<ref>{{cite web|url=https://www.etonline.com/dancing-with-the-stars-hypes-up-disney-plus-move-in-glittery-new-promo-exclusive-189301|title=''Dancing With the Stars'' Hypes Up Disney Plus Move in Glittery New Promo (Exclusive)|work=[[Entertainment Tonight]]|author=Philiana Ng|date=August 18, 2022|access-date=August 18, 2022|archive-date=August 18, 2022|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20220818171918/https://www.etonline.com/dancing-with-the-stars-hypes-up-disney-plus-move-in-glittery-new-promo-exclusive-189301|url-status=live}}</ref> [[Britt Stewart]], [[Peta Murgatroyd]], [[Emma Slater]], [[Koko Iwasaki]], [[Val Chmerkovskiy]], [[Alan Bersten]], [[Gleb Savchenko]], and [[Louis van Amstel]] were later revealed to be the rest of the professional dancers for the season.<ref>{{cite web|url=https://heavy.com/entertainment/dancing-with-the-stars/season-31-pros-roster-lineup/|title=Every ''Dancing With the Stars'' Season 31 Professional Dancer Revealed|work=[[Heavy (website)|Heavy]]|author=Beth Heyn|date=August 30, 2022|access-date=August 31, 2022|archive-date=August 31, 2022|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20220831022925/https://heavy.com/entertainment/dancing-with-the-stars/season-31-pros-roster-lineup/|url-status=live}}</ref> [[Mark Ballas]] was announced as a pro on September 8.<ref name="Ballas">{{cite web|url=https://www.usmagazine.com/entertainment/news/mark-ballas-returns-to-dwts-for-season-31-after-5-year-hiatus/|title=Mark Ballas Returns to ''Dancing With the Stars'' for Season 31 After 5-Year Absence|work=[[Us Magazine]]|author=Michelle McGahan|date=September 8, 2022|access-date=September 8, 2022}}</ref> [[Sasha Farber]] was initially reported to be a troupe member this season, but was later revealed to also be returning as a pro.<ref>{{cite web | url=https://heavy.com/entertainment/dancing-with-the-stars/fans-upset-sasha-farber-troupe-announcement/ | title=Fans Outraged After 'Dancing with the Stars' Pro is 'Demoted' | date=2 September 2022 | last1=Heyn | first1=Beth | access-date=September 9, 2022 | archive-date=September 9, 2022 | archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20220909143130/https://heavy.com/entertainment/dancing-with-the-stars/fans-upset-sasha-farber-troupe-announcement/ | url-status=live }}</ref><ref>{{cite web | url=https://heavy.com/entertainment/dancing-with-the-stars/sasha-farber-season-31-partner-celebrity/ | title=Sasha Farber's 'Dancing with the Stars' Season 31 Partner Revealed | date=8 September 2022 | access-date=September 9, 2022 | archive-date=September 9, 2022 | archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20220909143129/https://heavy.com/entertainment/dancing-with-the-stars/sasha-farber-season-31-partner-celebrity/ | url-status=live }}</ref> Three pro dancers from the previous season did not return, [[Jenna Johnson (dancer)|Jenna Johnson]], [[Sharna Burgess]], and [[Lindsay Arnold]]. Johnson was pregnant with her first child at the time, while Arnold wanted to spend time with her family.<ref>{{cite web|url=https://www.usmagazine.com/celebrity-moms/news/jenna-johnson-is-pregnant-expecting-1st-child-with-val-chmerkovskiy/|title=''DWTS'' Pro Jenna Johnson Is Pregnant, Expecting 1st Child With Husband Val Chmerkovskiy|work=[[Us Magazine]]|author=Meredith Nardino|date=July 15, 2022|access-date=August 31, 2022|archive-date=August 19, 2022|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20220819165644/https://www.usmagazine.com/celebrity-moms/news/jenna-johnson-is-pregnant-expecting-1st-child-with-val-chmerkovskiy/|url-status=live}}</ref><ref>{{cite web|url=https://heavy.com/entertainment/dancing-with-the-stars/lindsay-arnold-return-back-leaving/|title=Fan-Favorite Professional Dancer Not Returning for DWTS Season 31|work=[[Heavy (website)|Heavy]]|author=Beth Heyn|date=August 29, 2022|access-date=August 31, 2022|archive-date=August 30, 2022|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20220830072621/https://heavy.com/entertainment/dancing-with-the-stars/lindsay-arnold-return-back-leaving/|url-status=live}}</ref> Iwasaki, who was the runner-up on [[So You Think You Can Dance (American TV series) season 14|season 14]] of ''[[So You Think You Can Dance (American TV series)|So You Think You Can Dance]]'' and performed as part of the ''Dancing with the Stars Live! – 2022 Tour'', joined the show as a first-time pro.

On September 26, 2022, it was announced that Daniella Karagach had [[COVID-19]] and would miss that night's performance. [[Alexis Warr]] replaced her as Joseph Baena's dance partner for two weeks.<ref name="Daniella COVID">{{cite web|url=https://deadline.com/2022/09/dancing-with-the-stars-daniella-karagach-tests-positive-for-covid-1235127358/|title=''Dancing With the Stars'': Pro Daniella Karagach Tests Positive for Covid; Will Miss Tonight's Performance|work=[[Deadline Hollywood]]|author=Lynette Rice|date=September 26, 2022|access-date=September 26, 2022|archive-date=September 26, 2022|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20220926184218/https://deadline.com/2022/09/dancing-with-the-stars-daniella-karagach-tests-positive-for-covid-1235127358/|url-status=live}}</ref> On October 28, 2022, it was announced that Val Chmerkovskiy had COVID-19 and would miss the October 31 episode. Alan Bersten filled in for him as Gabby Windey's partner for the episode.<ref name="Val COVID">{{cite web|url=https://www.instagram.com/p/CkRThlnysgH/|title=Sending well wishes for a fast recovery to @valentin. He has tested positive for COVID and will not be performing in Monday's…|author=dancingwiththestars|author-link=Dancing with the Stars (American TV series)|via=[[Instagram]]|date=October 28, 2022|access-date=October 28, 2022}}</ref>

On November 20, 2022, professional dancer Cheryl Burke announced her retirement from the show after 26 seasons.<ref>{{cite web|url=https://people.com/tv/dwts-cheryl-burke-says-goodbye-after-26-seasons-exclusive/|title=Cheryl Burke Is Saying Goodbye to ''DWTS'' After 26 Seasons: 'I Have Been Crying Nonstop'|work=[[People (magazine)|People]]|author=Lanae Brody|date=November 20, 2022|access-date=November 21, 2022|archive-date=November 20, 2022|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20221120215152/https://people.com/tv/dwts-cheryl-burke-says-goodbye-after-26-seasons-exclusive/|url-status=live}}</ref>

