===Host and judges===
On July 14, 2022, it was announced that [[Tyra Banks]] would return as host, with [[Len Goodman]], [[Derek Hough]], [[Carrie Ann Inaba]], and [[Bruno Tonioli]] returning as judges. Additionally, it was announced that [[Dancing with the Stars (American TV series) season 19|season nineteen]] champion [[Alfonso Ribeiro]] would be joining the show alongside Banks as co-host.<ref name="Ribeiro cohost" /><ref>{{cite web|url=https://deadline.com/2022/07/dancing-with-the-stars-adds-alfonso-ribeiro-co-host-tyra-banks-1235063811/|title=''Dancing With The Stars'' Adds Alfonso Ribeiro As Co-Host; Tyra Banks To Return To Ballroom|work=[[Deadline Hollywood]]|author=Lynette Rice|date=July 14, 2022|access-date=August 3, 2022|archive-date=August 3, 2022|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20220803212635/https://deadline.com/2022/07/dancing-with-the-stars-adds-alfonso-ribeiro-co-host-tyra-banks-1235063811/|url-status=live}}</ref> On October 24, [[Michael Bublé]] served as a guest judge.<ref name="Bublé guest judge">{{cite web|url=https://www.tvinsider.com/1066148/dancing-with-the-stars-michael-buble-night-dances-guest-judge/|title=What to Expect From Michael Bublé Night on ''Dancing With the Stars''|work=[[TV Insider]]|author=Eve Vawter|date=October 19, 2022|access-date=October 24, 2022}}</ref>

During the semifinals, Goodman announced that this would be his final season as a judge.<ref name="Goodman retirement">{{cite web|url=https://people.com/tv/dancing-with-the-stars-head-judge-len-goodman-is-retiring/|title=''Dancing with the Stars'' Head Judge Len Goodman Announces His Retirement: 'Hasta La Vista Baby!'|work=[[People (magazine)|People]]|author=Joelle Goldstein|date=November 14, 2022|access-date=November 17, 2022|archive-date=November 17, 2022|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20221117012801/https://people.com/tv/dancing-with-the-stars-head-judge-len-goodman-is-retiring/|url-status=live}}</ref>

=== Dance troupe ===
The dance troupe returned for season 31 after being absent for the previous three seasons and consisted of returning pro [[Ezra Sosa]] and new pros Kateryna Klishyna, [[Alexis Warr]], and D'Angelo Castro.<ref>{{cite web|url=https://heavy.com/entertainment/dancing-with-the-stars/artem-chigvintsev-season-31-partner-celebrity/|title=Artem Chigvintsev Season 31 ''Dancing With the Stars'' Partner Revealed|work=[[Heavy (website)|Heavy]]|author=Beth Heyn|date=September 8, 2022|access-date=September 8, 2022|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20230111043700/https://heavy.com/entertainment/dancing-with-the-stars/artem-chigvintsev-season-31-partner-celebrity/|archive-date=January 11, 2023}}</ref>

